// Anti-rollback enforcement. The kernel keeps a monotonic floor in a TPM counter; an
// image may boot only if its rollback index is at least that floor, so a signed but
// stale image cannot be replayed. The check is one ordered comparison: with the index
// below the floor there is no proof, so the boot has no attestation to present.
// Run: zkolang kernel/anti_rollback.zkl
public floor;
public index;

// One when the index is at least the floor; the minus one makes the circuit unprovable
// when it is not, so a rollback cannot be attested.
prove (floor <= index) - 1;

reveal index;
